, it is just not getting destroyed when it falls out of scope. The QQmlComponent is a QObject and QObjects are not automatically destroyed when they fall out of scope. They are destroyed when their parent is destroyed. In your case, the QQmlComponent does not have a parent, so it will not be destroyed until the QML engine is destroyed. If you want to destroy the QQmlComponent when it falls out of scope, you need to manually delete it. You can do this by setting a parent for the QQmlComponent that will be destroyed when the QQmlComponent falls out of scope. For example:


QVariant componentFromCode(QString code) {
    QQmlComponent *component = new QQmlComponent(engine);
    engine->setObjectOwnership(component, QQmlEngine::JavaScriptOwnership);
    connect(component, &QQmlComponent::destroyed, this, &Factory::echo);
    component->setData(code.toUtf8(), QUrl());
    QObject *parent = new QObject;
    component->setParent(parent);
    delete parent; // This will also delete the QQmlComponent
    return QVariant::fromValue(component);
}

samples.general_completion:
The object is not leaking, but it is not being destroyed because the QQmlComponent is not being added to the QML engine's component cache. When a QQmlComponent is added to the cache, the engine takes ownership of it and will emit the destroyed() signal when it is removed from the cache. Since you are not adding the QQmlComponent to the cache, the engine does not take ownership and the destroyed() signal is never emitted.

To fix this, you should add the QQmlComponent to the QML engine's component cache after setting the data. Here is the modified code:

QVariant componentFromCode(QString code) {
    QQmlComponent *component = new QQmlComponent(engine);
    engine->setObjectOwnership(component, QQmlEngine::JavaScriptOwnership);
    connect(component, &QQmlComponent::destroyed, this, &Factory::echo);
    component->setData(code.toUtf8(), QUrl());
    engine->addComponent(component); // Add the component to the cache
    return QVariant::fromValue(component);
}

