You can't do that. Interfaces are not classes, and they don't work the same way. Interfaces are a contract, not a blueprint. You can't "override" a method in an interface, because interfaces don't have implementations.

What you can do is create a new interface that extends the old one and adds new methods. But you can't change the old methods.

If you want to change the behavior of a method, you need to do that in the class that implements the interface.

In your case, you could create a new interface:

interface iShipper {
    public function __construct($vendors_no = null, $shipment = null);
    // other methods...
}

