One way to solve this issue is to create a custom pipe that will handle the conversion from decimal to percentage. Here's how you can do it:

```typescript
@Pipe({name: 'decimalToPercent'})
export class DecimalToPercentPipe implements PipeTransform {
  transform(value: number, args?: any): string {
    if (args && args.precision) {
      const precision = parseInt(args.precision, 10);
      return `${(value * 100).toFixed(precision)}%`;
    } else {
      return `${(value * 100).toFixed(2)}%`;
    }
  }
}
```

Then, you can use this custom pipe in your template like this:

```html
{{data.value | decimalToPercent: '1.0'}}
```

This will display the value as a percentage with the specified precision. If no precision is provided, it will default to 2 decimal places. This way, you can control the precision of the percentage display and avoid getting 100% when the value is 1.0.

