```dart
void stopListeningToUSBStream() {
  usbStream.cancel(); // Stop listening to the broadcast stream
  await USBSerialSingleton.instance.port.close(); // Close the underlying port
}

// Call this method when you want to stop receiving messages
stopListeningToUSBStream();
```

By closing the port, you ensure that no more data will be received from the USB serial device, even if you have multiple subscriptions to the broadcast stream. This way, you can effectively stop receiving messages on your `onDataReceivedFromUSBSerial` method.

